title Caravan ladder fold M -- the largest fold this arc has taken, and the printed queue that chose it
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, Standfast on reds first, and send it as its own signed round.
think Standfast first. The ledger's only live row is REDS %103, whose repair is already designed -- the operator card's Git nib is corrected in the working tree and rides the next work commit, since a pin-only follow-up is what the rule exists to refuse. That repair is this round's send, so the red closes by doing rather than by claiming.
think The rota doc this lap is item 11, active-designing/20260618-182412_single-stranded.md. It reads as though written for this fold. Simple and easy are different axes; a part that stands free can be drawn out, understood, and changed alone. Thirty-seven copies of one body are not thirty-seven free parts -- they are one part written thirty-seven times, and each copy is a place a fault can hide. Lifting the body once makes it single-stranded in the sense the brief means.
think The crux was already named by measurement rather than by hand. The fourth meter, born on the lap before this one, printed mend_the_plan at the head of its queue -- 36 rungs by 178 lines, 6,230 carried. Ran the scan on metal first rather than trusting the card, and it agreed exactly.
think Then a hand looked, and found what the meter could not. Forty files declare mend_the_plan; thirty-six share one exact text. Of the four that differ, three are genuinely earlier rungs with less to do -- appraise at 146 lines, bear at 116, mend at 91. The fourth, recant, differs in two lines out of a hundred and seventy-eight: it reaches report_out.recanted directly where every rung above reaches recanting_of(report_out).recanted.
think That is because recant.rye IS the recanting tier -- its own Report carries the recanted field. So the accessor every rung above uses to climb down to it has no meaning there, and was never written. Naming it anyway, as a three-line identity returning the report itself, makes recant's body byte-identical to the other thirty-six. Fold J learned this on the staircase; it holds again, and this time it is worth 178 more lines.
think Audited the reach before moving a line, as every fold in this arc has. Thirty-eight symbols are named in the body; twenty-five already stood pub from earlier folds. Twelve wanted widening -- Table, standing, appraising_of, abandoning_of, below_of, bearing_of, recanting_of, run_of, and the four spine bodies the repair runs. 427 widenings in all, and each one only widens, so the edit cannot narrow anything.
think One false alarm in the audit worth recording: max_queue_len and max_in_flight read as MISSING in all thirty-seven because my grep pattern wanted a space or paren after the name and those two carry a type annotation. Read the declaration rather than the grep, and both were already pub. A pattern that cannot see its subject answers in the voice of one that can -- REDS %102's family in miniature, caught by reading rather than by trusting.
think Lifted the body into caravan/ladder_checks.rye as one comptime body taking the rung, with every rung symbol reached through it. Prefixed only the code half of each line, splitting off the // comment first, so the body's heavy prose -- which uses words like standing and reseated in their ordinary English sense -- stayed untouched. Each rung keeps a nineteen-line delegate.
think Proved it the way this arc proves things rather than by reading the diff. Built and ran the top rung, then the whole choir cold: 99 GREEN. tame_style_check bans clean, width-check clean, the ladder reach guard holding at one rung below per rung.
obs The carry falls 142,850 to 137,140 -- a drop of 5,710 rather than the 6,408 lifted, and the difference is honest and worth naming. The thirty-seven shims are themselves byte-identical, so they carry 36 x 19 = 684 lines of their own; and widening fn fill_table to pub fn fill_table changed those thirty-seven bodies' text, splitting that family from 43 rungs to 37 in the meter's eyes. A fold pays a small carry back and reshapes the families beside it. The meter reports what is true rather than what is flattering.
obs 6,403 lines deleted for 747 of harness and call, 5,488 lines off disk. More than three times fold L, which was itself the largest to that point. The queue named it, and the queue was right.
obs The two rows a lift could most easily have inflated stood still for the ninth fold running -- the byte-identical check carry at 47 and the orchestration spine at 0. A cost removed rather than traded, nine laps in a row.
obs The fourth meter earned itself on the lap after it was born. Fold L took six folds and a hand to find; fold M took one line of printed output. That is the whole argument for printing a queue rather than remembering one.
obs A fold's own widening puts the next folds in view, and this lap made that structural rather than incidental. fill_table at 2,484 across 37 rungs, reap_oldest at 1,716 across 40, and settle_the_plan at 1,645 across 36 all stand pub now because this body reached them -- three future folds whose reach is already verified.
obs The meter's standing limit, named plainly rather than left to surprise a later lap: it compares exact text, so a body that is NEARLY alike is invisible until a hand looks. recant.rye is the first instance found. The answer each time is the same cheap move -- an accessor born for the tier the rung owns.
obs The disk-line row in caravan/README.md re-measured both endpoints this lap with one command rather than carrying fold L's number forward, and they disagree with that note by 168 lines. Rather than relitigate a dated number, the table states its method and stands on what it measured -- REDS %93, a tally repeated from memory drifts.
obs The rota doc reads as though written for the round. Single-stranded says the reward of free-standing parts is the freedom to change course, and reliability follows because a fault has fewer places to hide. Thirty-seven copies were thirty-seven places; there is one now.
loom witness=caravan_suite_witness rungs=99 wall_s=406 verdict=green
